This tool uses, without vendoring, the following third-party software. Each is installed at a
pinned version when the tool is set up, and keeps its own licence and notices.

HyperFrames (the video format's renderer)
  https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes, npm package "hyperframes", pinned in
  src/publishing/hyperframes/package.json and package-lock.json.
  By HeyGen (heygen-com) and the HyperFrames contributors. Licensed under the Apache License,
  Version 2.0: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
  Its own credits (CREDITS.md in that repository) acknowledge Remotion as prior art and the
  open-source projects it builds on, including Puppeteer, FFmpeg, GSAP and Hono. The publishing
  video format does not load GSAP: its motion is CSS animation.

Node.js (runs HyperFrames), via the PyPI package nodejs-wheel-binaries, pinned in uv.lock.
  https://nodejs.org, MIT licence and the third-party licences it ships.

Playwright and Chromium (the PDF and video renderer), pinned in uv.lock.
  https://playwright.dev, Apache License 2.0; Chromium, BSD-style licence and its third-party notices.

PDFium (page images and thumbnails: render-html, render-md, pdf-pages, build --png, compare), via the
  PyPI package pypdfium2, pinned in uv.lock. https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium, BSD-3-Clause;
  pypdfium2 https://github.com/pypdfium2-team/pypdfium2, Apache-2.0 or BSD-3-Clause.

pandoc (the pandoc engine of convert), pinned in src/publishing/pandoc.py with the sha256 of each release.
  https://pandoc.org, by John MacFarlane and contributors, GPL-2.0-or-later. Run as a separate program,
  not linked or vendored.

TeX Live (pdfLaTeX, for PDFs from pandoc), Debian's texlive-latex-base, texlive-latex-recommended,
  texlive-fonts-recommended and lmodern in Dockerfile.pandoc. https://tug.org/texlive, free software under
  the licences of each package.

FFmpeg (video encoding), from the host or the container's Debian package; LGPL/GPL per build.
  https://ffmpeg.org

Noto fonts (vendored in src/publishing/theme/fonts/), SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL.txt there).
